Subject: [PATCH] udp: normalise outer checksum when re-segmenting a UDP tunnel GSO skb

A UDP tunnel GSO skb produced by an earlier segmentation pass (for example
skb_segment() splitting a GRO frag_list skb into several GSO skbs on a
device without NETIF_F_FRAGLIST) has encap_hdr_csum set and carries a
completed outer UDP checksum. When a lower device segments it again in
software, __skb_udp_tunnel_segment() treats that value as the
pseudo-header seed and every resulting segment gets a wrong outer UDP
checksum. Rewrite the field to the seed before it is consumed.

See docs/REPORT.md in this repository for the analysis and reproducer.

